'''Gat Blu''' is a [[Balboa|Balboan]] {{w|VTuber|virtual YouTuber}} and virtual musician. She is the most subscribed Balboan VTuber on [[VideoMes]], with approximately 2.1 million subscribers as of 2026, and is one of the most recognisable virtual entertainers in the {{w|Volisanian language|Volisanian-speaking}} world. Her content consists primarily of {{w|Let's Play|gaming streams}} and original {{w|electronic dance music|EDM}} releases.

Gat Blu's character design is a blue-haired {{w|catgirl|cat-girl}} with cat ears and a tail, dressed in a casual hoodie and headphones. The character has no elaborate backstory; the performer has described the concept as "just a blue cat who plays games and makes music."

== Career ==

=== Debut and early growth (2020–2021) ===

Gat Blu debuted on [[VideoMes]] on 14 November 2020. Her earliest content consisted of gaming streams in [[Volisanian language|Volisanian]] playing popular titles, with a focus on {{w|first-person shooter}} and {{w|rhythm game}} genres. The streams were informal and comedy-oriented, with the performer adopting a playful, self-deprecating persona that contrasted with the more polished presentation of larger VTuber agencies.

Her channel grew steadily through 2021, aided by clips of her comedic reactions being shared across [[VideoMes]] and other Volisanian-language social media. By the end of 2021, she had reached 300,000 subscribers.

=== Breakthrough and music career (2022–2023) ===

In early 2022, Gat Blu began releasing original electronic music, starting with the single "Llum Blava" (Blue Light), an {{w|electronic dance music|EDM}} track produced in collaboration with an unnamed Balboan producer. The track was used as intro music for her streams and was released on [[VideoMes]] as a music video featuring her character model. "Llum Blava" became a viral hit in the Volisanian-speaking world, reaching 4 million views within two months.

The success of "Llum Blava" led to a series of single releases throughout 2022 and 2023, including "Neó" (Neon), "Freqüència" (Frequency), and "Corrent" (Current). Her music style is characterised by upbeat {{w|synth-pop}} melodies, {{w|bass house}} drops, and Volisanian-language vocals. Several of her tracks were used in {{w|esports}} tournament montages and gaming highlight reels on [[VideoMes]], broadening her audience beyond the VTuber community.

By mid-2023, Gat Blu had surpassed 1 million subscribers on [[VideoMes]], making her the most subscribed Balboan VTuber and one of the most popular Volisanian-language virtual entertainers. She began streaming occasional sessions in [[Zong language|Zong]], citing a growing audience in [[Zong]] and other Zongese-speaking regions.

=== Peak and controversy (2024–2025) ===

Gat Blu reached 2 million subscribers in early 2024. She released her first extended play, ''Estats del Corrent'' (Current States), in March 2024, a six-track collection of EDM and {{w|future bass}} tracks. The EP was streamed over 10 million times on [[VideoMes]] in its first month.

In June 2025, Gat Blu was involved in a controversy regarding her vocal performances. A former collaborator alleged that several of her "live" vocal performances during streaming events had used {{w|AI music|AI-generated vocals}} rather than the performer's own singing voice, and that the vocal tracks on her released singles had been substantially enhanced or replaced by AI vocal synthesis. The allegations were published on [[VideoMes]] and widely discussed across Volisanian-language social media.

Gat Blu acknowledged that she had used AI vocal processing on her released tracks, stating that she had never claimed the studio recordings were unprocessed. She denied using AI vocals during live performances, though some listeners produced audio analysis suggesting otherwise. The controversy divided her audience: some viewers argued that vocal processing was standard in electronic music production, while others felt that the emphasis on "live singing" in her promotional material had been misleading.

The controversy resulted in a temporary decline in subscribers and a hiatus from streaming during July and August 2025. She returned to streaming in September 2025 with a new vocal setup and a statement committing to transparency about her use of vocal processing.

== Content ==

Gat Blu's content is divided between gaming streams and music. Her gaming streams typically run two to three hours and feature a mix of competitive multiplayer games, {{w|visual novel}}s, and reaction content. She is known for her comedic commentary and frequent interaction with chat.

Her music releases are primarily in the {{w|electronic dance music}} genre, with influences from {{w|bass house}}, {{w|future bass}}, and {{w|synth-pop}}. All of her released tracks feature Volisanian-language vocals. She has not performed live concerts, though she has expressed interest in a virtual concert format.

== Character and design ==

<!-- NOTE: Image filename is "Gat Blau" (original spelling) — do not rename, images already uploaded -->
[[File:Gat Blau full body.png|250px|thumb|Full-body character model, showing the default outfit]]

Gat Blu's character is a blue-haired cat-girl with light blue cat ears and a matching tail. Her default outfit consists of a white hoodie with blue accents, {{w|over-ear headphones}}, and a cat-shaped badge on her chest. The design was created by an independent illustrator whose identity has not been publicly disclosed.

The character has no established backstory or fictional lore. The performer has stated in streams that she chose a cat-girl design because she "liked cats and liked blue" and that she did not want to build an elaborate fictional persona, preferring to be herself behind an avatar.

